{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v2","paper":"erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface","excerpts":[["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:B11-inv","Diagonal certificates through <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>82</mn></math></span>","<p><em> The current aggregate\nestablishes </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>82</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟹</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>P</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> where <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>t</mi></math></span> is the diagonal certificate\npredicate in Proposition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#prop:B3\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:B3\">6.72</a>. The earlier aggregate\ncovered 28 explicit cases through <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>64</mn></math></span>, including <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>17</mn></math></span>; the later\ntheorem fills the gaps and extends the range through <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>82</mn></math></span>. Each instance reduces to exact finite\narithmetic with the displayed totient values, using the prime-power\nfactorisations and Lucas primality certificates in the source. This\nproves neither <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>83</mn></math></span> nor infinitely\nmany instances, and therefore does not establish the quantified\nconditions in Propositions <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#prop:A10\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:A10\">6.71</a>, <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#prop:B3\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:B3\">6.72</a> and <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#prop:B7\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:B7\">6.73</a>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:C1-inv","A coprime-pair expression for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span>","<p><em> For <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, the number of integer pairs <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. Indeed, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. The boundary case\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> contributes <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>; it disappears when both\ncoordinates are required to be positive. Consequently, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mtable columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"0.1em\"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></munder><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nFor independent random variables <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">Pr</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">Pr</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, the left side is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">Pr</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. Thus <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> has a coprimality-probability\ninterpretation. This identity does not supply an estimate for the binary\ndigits or tail residues used elsewhere in the paper.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:values-exponents-one-two","The values at exponents one and two","<p><em> The first two values are <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:first-two-summands-give-positive","The first two summands give a positive\nHankel gap","<p><em> <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></span>, so the rational sequence\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></math></span> is strictly log-concave\nfor every integer <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:strict-log-concavity-all-integer","Strict log-concavity for all integer\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>","<p><em> For every integer\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nEquivalently, the determinant of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"1\"><mtable columnspacing=\"0.333em\" rowspacing=\".2em\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></math></span> is\nnegative. The two-summand comparison gives an elementary proof, detailed\nbelow; the same strict inequality is also proved in Lean.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:binary-carry-criterion","Integer recurrence criterion for a\nbinary series","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> satisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span>. Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math></span> is rational if and\nonly if there are an integer <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>v</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>\nand an integer sequence <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>u</mi></math></span> such that\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟶</mo><mn>0.</mn></math></span></div>\n<p><em> For each fixed <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>v</mi></math></span>, such a sequence is unique and equals\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:uniqueness-under-growth-condition","Uniqueness under the growth\ncondition","<p><em> A real sequence <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi></math></span>\nwith <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is identically zero.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:exact-rational-approximation-formula","An exact rational approximation\nformula","<p><em> For integers <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, with the integer prefixes <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></math></span> defined above, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" columnalign=\"right left\" columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"3pt\" data-break-align=\"bottom top\" minlabelspacing=\"0em\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mi></mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em> This follows by substituting the\nsquared-denominator identity for <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span>\ninto <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></math></span>.\nThere is no required ordering between <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:geometric-tail-bound","A geometric tail bound","<p><em> For\nevery integer <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mrow><mo>|</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Indeed, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≥</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. The sum of the resulting geometric\nmajorant is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:sum-over-divisor-indices","The sum over divisor indices","<p><em>\nFor integers <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, the part of the Möbius expansion\nindexed by divisors of <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi></math></span> is </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mtable columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"0.1em\"><mtr><mtd><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>H</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>s</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></munder><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mfrac><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> This is the\nstandard identity <span class=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></munder><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></math></span> at <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. The formal statement\nwrites the same value after extracting <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, where <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>rad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></munder><mi>p</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:divisor-sum-complement","The divisor sum and its\ncomplement","<p><em> For integers <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" columnalign=\"right left\" columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"3pt\" data-break-align=\"bottom top\" minlabelspacing=\"0em\"><mtr><mtd><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>+</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mtable columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"0.1em\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>d</mi><mo>∤</mo><mi>H</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></munder><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>.</mo></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Here <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow></math></span> is the indicator of the stated\ndivisibility condition. The identity follows by expanding both totients\nas <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></math></span> and separating the indices <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>H</mi></math></span>. Such an index divides either\nendpoint precisely when it divides <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>s</mi></math></span>, and its difference is then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:doubling-full-totient-difference","Doubling the full totient difference","<p><em> For nonnegative integers <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></math></span>\nwith <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi></math></span> even, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\".2em\" columnalign=\"left left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>r</mi><mtext> even</mtext><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>r</mi><mtext> odd</mtext><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\" symmetric=\"true\"></mo></mrow></math></span></div>\n<p><em> This applies to the full difference, not just its\ndivisor contribution. It follows from <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> for even <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> for odd <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:doubling-identity-two-portions-sum","A doubling identity for two\nportions of the sum","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>∤</mo><mi>H</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></math></span>. The <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi></math></span>-summands in the complementary sums at\noffsets <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>s</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi></math></span> are, respectively, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> For the second expression, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>∤</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi></math></span>; otherwise <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi></math></span> would divide their difference <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi></math></span>. Thus the second contribution is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> times the first, including the zero\ncase <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. The two terms have\ndifferent binary weights in a window sum, so this identity alone is not\na cancellation of their weighted contributions.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:positive-coefficients-numerator-polynomial","Positive coefficients of the numerator\npolynomial","<p><em> For a squarefree integer <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, the numerator polynomial has the\nexplicit expression </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></munder><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Every\ncoefficient for <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></math></span> is\npositive, and the higher coefficients are zero. Extracting <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></math></span> on the left gives <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></munder><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></math></span>, which\nproves the formula. The squarefree assumption identifies this divisor\nsum with the subset-of-primes definition in the formal source.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#cor:numerator-polynomial-explicit-positive-coefficients","","<p><em> For the same squarefree <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi></math></span>, evaluation at <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> gives the integer </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></munder><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Each quotient is an integer because\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>r</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:geometric-remainder-bound","The geometric remainder bound","<p><em> The remainder after the first two geometric terms of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>8</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msup><mn>8</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Indeed, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span>. Summing over <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>m</mi></math></span>, for an integer <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, gives </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mn>8</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>21</mn></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msup><mn>8</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"]],"source":"erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.json?v=e6abdbcd8877"}
